{
  "id": "495502cc-c826-4a1e-8419-a8588302cf83",
  "page_title": "'Quickstart: Use Azure OpenAI Service with the JavaScript SDK and the completions API'",
  "page_description": "Walkthrough on how to get started with Azure OpenAI and make your first completions call with the Go SDK.",
  "page_date": "08/30/2023",
  "chunk_title": "Create a sample application",
  "chunk_content": "Create a sample application   Create a new file named completions.go. Copy the following code into the completions.go file.  ```go package main  import ( \t\"context\" \t\"fmt\" \t\"os\"  \t\"github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/ai/azopenai\" \t\"github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/azcore/to\" )  func main() { \tazureOpenAIKey := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY\") \tmodelDeploymentID := \"gpt-35-turbo-instruct\"  \tazureOpenAIEndpoint := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT\")  \tif azureOpenAIKey == \"\" || modelDeploymentID == \"\" || azureOpenAIEndpoint == \"\" { \t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Skipping example, environment variables missing\\n\") \t\treturn \t}  \tkeyCredential, err := azopenai.NewKeyCredential(azureOpenAIKey)  \tif err != nil { \t\t// TODO: handle error \t}  \tclient, err := azopenai.NewClientWithKeyCredential(azureOpenAIEndpoint, keyCredential, nil)  \tif err != nil { \t\t// TODO: handle error \t}  \tresp, err := client.GetCompletions(context.TODO(), azopenai.CompletionsOptions{ \t\tPrompt:       []string{\"What is Azure OpenAI, in 20 words or less\"}, \t\tMaxTokens:    to.Ptr(int32(2048)), \t\tTemperature:  to.Ptr(float32(0.0)), \t\tDeployment: modelDeploymentID, \t}, nil)  \tif err != nil { \t\t// TODO: handle error \t}  \tfor _, choice := range resp.Choices { \t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Result: %s\\n\", *choice.Text) \t}  } ```  > [!IMPORTANT] > For production, use a secure way of storing and accessing your credentials like Azure Key Vault. For more information about credential security, see the Azure AI services security article.  Now open a command prompt and run:  ```cmd go mod init completions.go ```  Next run:  ```cmd go mod tidy ```  ```cmd go run completions.go ```",
